==Romani==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|lang=rom}} May have developed from {{der|rom|la|somnium}}. Compare Italian {{m|it|sogno}}, Istriot {{m|ist|sugno}}, cf. also Romanian {{m|ro|somn}}. Alternatively, pattern of overlap between Romani and Dardic languages may indicate cognate with Phalura sū, 'to sleep,' while that same overlap could also be explained by Wasi-Wari contact in what is modern day Afghanistan, with possible cognate Prasun {{m|prn|sǖ}}, 'dream.'

